{"id": "20503218", "revid": "10202399", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20503218", "title": "Doetinchem De Huet railway station", "text": "Doetinchem De Huet is a railway station located in western Doetinchem, Netherlands. The station lies between the quarters De Huet and Dichteren. The station was opened on 2 June 1985 as a replacement for the previous station \"Doetinchem West\" (earlier: \"Doetinchem-Wijnbergen\" (1885\u20131965)), which was open from 1885 to 1985. It's located on the Winterswijk\u2013Zevenaar railway. Train services are operated by Arriva and Breng. In a Railpro survey in 2005 there were approximately 1,232 passengers per day using Doetinchem De Huet station."}
