{"id": "20504982", "revid": "8570870", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20504982", "title": "French frigate Adrienne", "text": "Adrienne was a 46-gun frigate of the French Navy.\nOn 29 March 1811, she departed Toulon with \"Am\u00e9lie\", escorting the storeship \"Dromadaire\" carrying 8 tonnes of gunpowder and ammunition to Corfu. Two days later, the ships ran across a British squadron comprising HMS \"Unite\" and HMS \"Ajax\". \"Dromadaire\" was captured, while the frigates managed to escape to Portoferraio.\nShe was renamed to \"Aurore\" on 11 April 1814, to \"Dauphine\" on 5 September 1829, and to \"Aurore\" again on 9 August 1830."}
